{"kind": "local_or_unclassified_prose", "line": 15764, "review_required": true, "scope_stack": [], "text_excerpt": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes over a base scheme $S$. Let $Z \\subset Y$ be the scheme theoretic image of $f$, see Morphisms, Section \\ref{morphisms-section-scheme-theoretic-image}. Let $g : S' \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes and let $f' : X \\times_S S' \\to Y \\times_S S'$ be the base change of $f$ by $g$. It is not always true that $Z \\times_S S' \\subset Y \\times_S S'$ is the scheme theoretic image of $f'$. Let us say that {\\it formation of the scheme theoretic image of $f/S$ commutes with arbitrary base change} if for every $g$ as above the scheme theoretic image of $f'$ is equal to $Z \\times_S S'$."}
